    "description": "Wavefront Studio builds websites, SEO and lead systems for small businesses across Florida, from our base in Sarasota.",
    "content": "<p>Wavefront Studio builds websites, SEO and lead systems for small businesses across Florida, from our base in Sarasota.</p>\n<div class=\"lf-cta\"><p>Not sure how you rank in Florida right now?</p><p>We will audit your site for free and tell you what is actually holding it back in Florida — including if the answer is that you do not need a rebuild.</p><div class=\"lf-buttons\"><div class=\"lf-button\"><a class=\"lf-button-link\" href=\"/contact/\">Get a free audit</a></div><div class=\"lf-button\"><a class=\"lf-button-link\" href=\"tel:+19414152595\">Call (941) 415-2595</a></div></div></div>\n<h2>An hour away, or it isn&#8217;t</h2>\n<p>We work out of 4363 Independence Ct in Sarasota, and the honest version of our service area is a circle, not a state. Businesses in Bradenton, Lakewood Ranch, Venice, Punta Gorda and the other Gulf Coast towns we already cover can sit across a table from us before anything gets built. If you are reading this page, your business almost certainly sits outside that circle.</p>\n<p>Beyond about an hour&#8217;s drive, we have no office there. All communication, project management and delivery happen digitally, the same as it would if you were in Pensacola or a different country. Distance inside Florida costs you nothing extra: we are on Eastern time with you unless you are in the western Panhandle, which runs on Central time, and nothing about how we work changes whether you are two hours up the road or across the state line.</p>\n<h2>The number that should decide how you compete online</h2>\n<p>Florida&#8217;s self-employment rate is 12.7%, against 9.9% nationally, roughly a quarter higher (American Community Survey 2024 one-year estimates). That is not a small gap, and it changes what a website is actually for here. Your site is not really competing against a handful of established firms. It is competing against a much larger number of one-person and small-crew operations offering something close to what you offer, often in your own town.</p>\n<p>A generic site that reads like a template does not stand out in a market this crowded. A site that names what you actually specialise in, shows real work and answers a specific search rather than a general one tends to do noticeably better here than the same site would in a state with fewer independent operators.</p>\n<h2>Where Florida genuinely differs from the rest of the country</h2>\n<p>Two other figures are worth knowing before anyone briefs you on a Florida-facing site. 23.4% of Floridians aged five and over speak Spanish at home, against 13.9% nationally, a meaningful gap even before you get to markets like Miami, where the figure runs much higher again. If a real share of your own customers are more comfortable in Spanish, a genuine bilingual page, not a machine translation bolted onto the English one, earns trust that an English-only site does not.</p>\n<p>Florida&#8217;s median age is 42.7, against 39.2 nationally, a state that skews a little older than the country as a whole. That argues for clear type and a phone number you do not have to hunt for, rather than a design built entirely around a 25-year-old&#8217;s phone habits. Broadband access and household income are close enough to the national figures that they should not change how a site gets built.</p>\n<h2>One state, several different markets</h2>\n<p>Florida is not a single market, and the mistake we see most often is a site built for the state name rather than the actual place. The western Panhandle, west of the Apalachicola River, runs on Central time, an hour behind the rest of the state. Brevard County, the Space Coast, is built around Kennedy Space Center and a cluster of aerospace and defence employers that includes SpaceX and Blue Origin. SpaceX alone expects its Starship operations to bring more than 600 new full-time jobs to the county by 2030. A business selling into that workforce needs a different vocabulary than one selling to retirees an hour away.</p>\n<p>North and Central Florida, around the university towns and the agricultural counties, are different markets again. The state drew a record 143.3 million visitors in 2025, but that number means something completely different to a hotel in Orlando than it does to a hardware store three hours north that rarely sees a tourist. South Florida runs through Miami&#8217;s port and airport into Latin America in a way nothing else in the state does, which is a large enough subject to get its own page rather than a paragraph here.</p>\n<p>The practical point: build your local search strategy around the actual place you operate, not the state. A site optimised for &#8220;Florida&#8221; competes with every other business in the state for a term almost nobody searches. A site built around your town and the two or three markets you genuinely serve competes for terms your customers actually type.</p>\n<h2>What we build</h2>\n<p><a href=\"/web-development/\">Websites</a> built to load fast on an ordinary Florida phone connection and to put your number where a stressed customer can find it in two seconds. <a href=\"/seo-service/\">SEO</a> built around your actual town rather than the state name, because that is what ranks. <a href=\"/lead-capture/\">Lead capture</a> and follow-up so an enquiry does not go quiet for three days. <a href=\"/ai-chatbot/\">AI chatbots</a> for businesses fielding the same five questions on repeat. And <a href=\"/digital-marketing/\">digital marketing</a> and <a href=\"/graphic-design/\">graphic design</a> for businesses that need the whole package rather than one piece of it.</p>\n<h2>Common questions</h2>\n<p><strong>Do you actually work with businesses this far from Sarasota?</strong> Yes. Most of Florida sits outside the hour we can reasonably drive, and remote is the default arrangement for this page, not an exception to it.</p>\n<p><strong>Will my site read like a template with my city swapped in?</strong> No. We build each site around what a specific business in a specific place needs. Not every town in Florida gets its own page here, but every client gets a plan built around their own market.</p>\n<p><strong>Do you build in Spanish as well as English?</strong> Yes, when it fits the business. Given how much of Florida operates in both languages, we treat a Spanish page as a real page, not an afterthought.</p>\n<p><strong>What does it cost?</strong> Websites start in the low five figures. SEO is monthly. We quote after a conversation.</p>\n<p><strong>Can you handle a business with locations in more than one Florida city?</strong> Yes, and it usually means each location gets its own page rather than one page trying to rank everywhere at once.</p>\n<h2>Talk to us</h2>\n<p>Call <strong>(941) 415-2595</strong>, email <strong>info@wavefrontstudiollc.com</strong>, or <a href=\"/contact/\">book a free consultation</a>. We are at 4363 Independence Ct, Sarasota, on Eastern time along with the rest of the state outside the western Panhandle.</p>\n<div class=\"lf-cta\"><div class=\"lf-buttons\"><div class=\"lf-button\"><a class=\"lf-button-link\" href=\"/contact/\">Get a free audit</a></div><div class=\"lf-button\"><a class=\"lf-button-link\" href=\"tel:+19414152595\">Call (941) 415-2595</a></div></div></div>\n<p>Nearby: <a href=\"/web-design-sarasota-fl/\">Sarasota</a> · <a href=\"/web-design-tampa-fl/\">Tampa</a> · <a href=\"/web-design-jacksonville-fl/\">Jacksonville</a> · <a href=\"/locations/\">all locations</a></p>\n<hr/>"
