    "description": "Wavefront Studio builds websites, SEO and lead systems for small businesses across Tennessee. We work with you remotely from Sarasota, Florida.",
    "content": "<p>Wavefront Studio builds websites, SEO and lead systems for small businesses across Tennessee. We work with you remotely from Sarasota, Florida.</p><div class=\"lf-cta\"><p>Not sure how you rank in Tennessee right now?</p><p>We will audit your site for free and tell you what is actually holding it back in Tennessee — including if the answer is that you do not need a rebuild.</p><div class=\"lf-buttons\"><div class=\"lf-button\"><a class=\"lf-button-link\" href=\"/contact/\">Get a free audit</a></div><div class=\"lf-button\"><a class=\"lf-button-link\" href=\"tel:+19414152595\">Call (941) 415-2595</a></div></div></div><h2>One state, two clocks, and why that matters before anything else</h2><p>We are not based in Tennessee, and the state itself complicates the question of what &#8220;nearby&#8221; even means. Tennessee is split between two time zones: Knoxville, Chattanooga and most of East Tennessee run on Eastern time, the same one Sarasota does, while Nashville, Memphis and the rest of Middle and West Tennessee run on Central time, an hour behind us.</p><p>Even East Tennessee is not entirely Eastern. Three counties on its western edge, Bledsoe, Cumberland and Marion, sit on Central time despite being geographically part of East Tennessee. In practice, how a call gets scheduled depends on exactly where in the state your business sits. Communication, project management and delivery all happen digitally regardless of which side of that line you are on.</p><h2>The number that matters: more of your customers are online by phone alone</h2><p>Ask how a Tennessee customer gets online, and for a real share the honest answer is a phone, and only a phone. 12.2% of Tennessee households have a smartphone as their only computing device, with no computer or tablet, against 9.9% nationally (American Community Survey 2024 one-year estimates).</p><p>Tennessee also has the highest share of households with no internet access at all among the states we cover here, at 5.5% against 4.5% nationally. Put together, a real portion of your customer base is finding you, if they find you at all, on a small screen and possibly on a slow connection. A site that is heavy, slow or hard to read on a phone is not a minor inconvenience in Tennessee. It is actively costing you customers who have no other way to reach you.</p><h2>Where Tennessee sits against the national numbers</h2><p>The rest of the picture is closer to average, though the income gap is worth noting. Median household income, at $71,997, runs about twelve per cent below the national $81,604, the widest gap among the states in this group, worth factoring into how you frame price on your site rather than assuming Nashville rates travel statewide.</p><p>Median age, at 39.1, sits almost exactly on the national 39.2. Spanish at home, at 5.8% of people aged five and over, is well below the national 13.9%, among the lowest of any state we cover. Self-employment, at 10.0% of workers, tracks the national rate closely. None of those numbers demands an unusual approach from you. The connectivity numbers above do.</p><h2>East, Middle and West Tennessee are three different economies</h2><p>Nashville is Middle Tennessee, and Middle Tennessee is not East or West Tennessee. Knoxville and Chattanooga anchor the eastern part of the state: Oak Ridge National Laboratory, one of the country&#8217;s largest Department of Energy research sites, has more than 4,400 employees outside Knoxville, and Chattanooga, despite the state&#8217;s connectivity numbers, is home to EPB, the municipal utility that made it the first city in the country with a community-wide gigabit fibre network in 2010 and was offering 10 gigabit speeds to every customer as a standard product by 2015, a genuine local exception to a statewide pattern.</p><p>The Great Smoky Mountains, straddling the Tennessee-North Carolina line near Gatlinburg, drew more than 11.5 million visits in 2025, more than any other national park in the country, feeding a tourism economy much of East Tennessee runs on. West Tennessee is Memphis, and Memphis is built around logistics: Memphis International Airport has for years ranked as the busiest cargo airport in North America, anchored by FedEx&#8217;s global superhub, which runs hundreds of flights through more than 80 miles of conveyor belts and sorts millions of packages a year. If your business sits in one of these three regions, you are not competing with, or selling to, the same people as a business in either of the other two.</p><h2>What we build</h2><p><a href=\"/web-development/\">Web design</a> built lean enough to load properly for the share of your customers online through a phone alone, not a desktop. <a href=\"/seo-service/\">SEO</a> targeted at your actual region, since Knoxville, Nashville and Memphis do not share a customer base or a search market. <a href=\"/lead-capture/\">Lead capture</a> that turns a phone call into a tracked, followed-up lead, since Tennessee customers are more likely than most to be calling from a phone in the first place. <a href=\"/custom-calculators/\">Custom calculators</a> and other interactive tools built to work properly at a smaller screen size rather than assuming everyone is on a laptop. And <a href=\"/graphic-design/\">graphic design</a> built around whichever of the state&#8217;s regional identities your customers actually recognise.</p><h2>Common questions</h2><p><strong>Do you have an office in Tennessee?</strong> No. We would work with you from Sarasota, Florida. Because the state splits across two time zones, which one applies to you depends on exactly where in Tennessee your business is.</p><p><strong>Are we in Eastern or Central time?</strong> If you are in Knoxville, Chattanooga or most of East Tennessee, Eastern, the same as us. If you are in Nashville, Memphis or most of Middle and West Tennessee, Central, an hour behind us.</p><p><strong>Does it matter that so many of our customers only have a phone for internet?</strong> Yes, directly. A site that is slow or hard to use on a small screen loses you a meaningful share of Tennessee customers who have no other way online, more than in most states we work with.</p><p><strong>Our business is in Memphis, not Nashville. Does that change your approach?</strong> Substantially. Memphis runs on logistics and freight, Nashville on hospitality and healthcare, and a plan built around one will not fit the other.</p><p><strong>What does it cost?</strong> Websites start in the low five figures. SEO is monthly. We quote after a conversation.</p><h2>Talk to us</h2><p>Call <strong>(941) 415-2595</strong>, email <strong>info@wavefrontstudiollc.com</strong>, or <a href=\"/contact/\">book a free consultation</a>. We are at 4363 Independence Ct, Sarasota, Florida.</p><div class=\"lf-cta\"><div class=\"lf-buttons\"><div class=\"lf-button\"><a class=\"lf-button-link\" href=\"/contact/\">Get a free audit</a></div><div class=\"lf-button\"><a class=\"lf-button-link\" href=\"tel:+19414152595\">Call (941) 415-2595</a></div></div></div><p>Nearby: <a href=\"/web-design-nashville-tn/\">Nashville</a> · <a href=\"/locations/\">all locations</a></p><hr/>"
